<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20981] ost_io and mdt_io threads ignore cpu_pattern CPT exclusions on single-CPT multi-NUMA hosts</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20981</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17501" title="specify libcfs CPT cpu_pattern to exclude NUMA cores" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17501"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17501&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; added X&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;...&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;/C&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;...&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; forms to cpu_pattern so selected cores can be excluded from Lustre's CPT table. The ost_io and mdt_io services don't honour that exclusion in one case: when the host has a single CPT and more than one NUMA node.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In that case ofd_oss.c and mdt_mds.c build a per-NUMA-node CPT table for the io services using cfs_cpt_set_node(). That call adds every core of the node, including cores that cpu_pattern removed. The excluded cores come back, and the io threads run on them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproducer:&lt;br/&gt;
1. On a host with 2 or more NUMA nodes, load libcfs with a cpu_pattern that gives one CPT and excludes one core. For example, cpu_pattern="N X&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;&amp;lt;cpu&amp;gt;&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;".&lt;br/&gt;
2. Start an OSS or MDS.&lt;br/&gt;
3. Check Cpus_allowed_list in /proc/&amp;lt;pid&amp;gt;/status for the ll_ost_io and mdt_io threads. It includes the excluded CPU.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
